From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:19:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6dsp-lpass-clocks: initialise the clocks before
 registering them

q6dsp_clock_dev_probe() sets the driver data after it has registered
every clock. Registering a clock can prepare it right away, when a
prepared orphan clock of a consumer is reparented to it, and the prepare
op reads the driver data. After an ADSP restart the old consumers still
hold such orphans, and the prepare dereferences a NULL q6dsp_cc.

Set the driver data before the first clock is registered, and start each
clock with the valid attribute LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO instead of
LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_INVALID, so an op run during registration sends a
valid attribute.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
index 03838582a..2ec6c2cf5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	cc->desc = desc;
 	cc->dev = dev;
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
@@ -159,6 +160,7 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 		clk->dev = dev;
 		clk->q6dsp_clk_id = q6dsp_clks[i].q6dsp_clk_id;
+		clk->attributes = LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_COUPLE_NO;
 		clk->rate = q6dsp_clks[i].rate;
 		clk->hw.init = &init;
 
@@ -178,8 +180,6 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
